{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 exit gate — confirmed parsimonious root-cause set:\n\n1. Completion orchestration defect (dynamic, confirmed): `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/completion-verification.yaml` routes every criterion through one aggregate agentic `verify` call; `src/rebar/llm/completion.py` raises that call to a 480-step floor, while `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` applies output and timeout limits per model request. There is no executable per-criterion termination boundary or fresh finalization turn. Runtime traces observed the predicted mechanism: repeated tool searches and ever-growing shared history, then a cap-filling non-JSON terminal response. Gold-context/no-tools finalization completed in 507 tokens, criterion isolation localized the runaway to individual criteria, affirmative prompt wording failed, and executable tool removal bounded exploration. Therefore verdict size, schema generation, one oversized ticket payload, and prompt wording alone are rejected alternatives.\n\n2. Failure-observability defect (dynamic + static, confirmed): `produce_completion_verdict()` constructs an inline `MemoryRecorder()` and discards it; the runner assigns usage only after `_pai_structured()` returns successfully; `UnretryableOutputError` bypasses that extraction. Live 16k/32k/64k failures consequently emitted only the generic raise-max_tokens message and no trace/request/tool metadata. The message is actively misleading for this mechanism and Pydantic AI also normalizes context overflow to `length`.\n\nDefect legitimacy: `verify_completion()` documents that it returns a validated PASS/FAIL completion_verdict or a typed LLM error, and the CLI promises to emit a PASS/FAIL verdict. The reported normal six-criterion leaf ticket instead exhausts the default path without a verdict, violating that contract. Classification: defect.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected post-fix behavior is a bounded, schema-valid verdict for recoverable exhaustion; irrecoverable exhaustion remains a typed fail-closed error with actionable bounded diagnostics/trace reference. Production callers (`completion._verify_completion_inner`, close precheck, CLI, opcert job, eval solver, criterion preview) consume only that public verdict-or-error contract. No caller depends on a single unbounded history, repeated searches, discarded recorder data, or the raise-max_tokens wording. Existing workflow tests that count one call are incidental shape checks for simple fixtures and can remain unchanged on the non-recovery path. Gate cleared.\n\nPhase 2 test contract card:\n- authoritative_contract: `completion.verify_completion` API docstring and CLI description require validated PASS/FAIL; bug acceptance criteria require bounded recovery, fail-closed exhaustion, diagnostics/trace metadata, and docs.\n- trigger_preconditions: a six-criterion completion request whose aggregate agent call raises token-cap exhaustion; bounded criterion calls can return complete structured records. A second fixture makes both aggregate and recovery paths exhaust.\n- production_path: `gate_dispatch.produce_completion_verdict` through the real completion workflow/reconcile seam with an injected stateful runner at the irreducible provider boundary.\n- test_tier: in-process workflow contract test; a runner unit test is too low because the defect is aggregate gate orchestration plus error propagation.\n- observable_postcondition: recoverable exhaustion returns one schema-valid PASS/FAIL covering every criterion without an env override; unrecoverable exhaustion raises, never PASSes, and persists actionable diagnostic evidence with a trace/reference.\n- negative_control: ordinary one-criterion completion still dispatches once and preserves existing verdict shape.\n- collateral_invariants: child precheck/reconcile semantics and public completion_verdict schema remain unchanged.\n- fault_injection: stateful runner raises the real typed truncation error at the workflow agent boundary, after confirming the request contains the multi-criterion fixture.\n- CI gate: exact held-out node plus `make test`/repository gates."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785180129480580001,"uuid":"eb1972a9-3e28-4a6e-9287-1853e666e874"}